Refuse a deferred hard link whose target goes through a symlink.
create_links_from_list() checks that the directories in a link's own
name are real directories, so that an archive cannot place a link
through a symlink it created, but not those in a hard link's target. An
archive with a symlink "dir" to an outside directory, followed by a hard
link to "dir/file", made the hard link to the outside file, which then
could be read or changed in place through the extracted tree. Check the
directories in the target of a hard link too.

---
 archival/libarchive/unsafe_symlink_target.c |    6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/archival/libarchive/unsafe_symlink_target.c
+++ b/archival/libarchive/unsafe_symlink_target.c
@@ -72,7 +72,11 @@
 		// SYMLINK_OUTSIDE_EXTRACT_DIR/etc/passwd sort of thing.
 		// (Our delayed creation of symlinks is not defending against it,
 		// we could create SYMLINK_OUTSIDE_EXTRACT_DIR ourself!)
-		if (!all_dir_components_are_dirs(linkname)) {
+		// The same goes for the target of a hardlink, which would
+		// otherwise link to a file outside, such as /etc/passwd.
+		if (!all_dir_components_are_dirs(linkname)
+		 || (list->data[0] && !all_dir_components_are_dirs(target))
+		) {
 			errno = ENOTDIR;
 			goto err;
 		}
